+# FAA intake and regional records for the April 2004 request
+
+**November 9, 2026 · B129 / PD01 / PD07.** Three FAA records from the National Archives separate the April 2004 request, the Eastern Region routing form and a folder labeled for Commission responses. The request copy supplies an assigned office, control number and mailing target that can be tested against an outgoing record. [NARA finding aid, boxes 111–112](https://www.archives.gov/research/foia/faa-finding-aid-108-126) · [Exact source pins](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## Incoming request and internal routing
+
+| Record | Observation | What remains open |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| AEA-2289, physical p. 1 | Dated **April 8, 2004**. Seeks the unclassified material already supplied by the FAA to the Commission, by delivery or inspection. The requester offered to address classification issues. The p. 1 routing stamp gives **AOA-10**, **04-4537** and a **5-17-04** mailing target. The body p. 1 lines 64–67 continues onto p. 2. | Original intake and assignment time, any extensions and the actual outgoing response. A routing target is an instruction. The stamp carries no verified date of dispatch. [NARA request, NAID 7600766](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7600766) |
+| AEA-2290, p. 1 | A separate internal cover sheet visibly gives **2004-004537-EA**. The **DUE DATE** field and seven visible pairs of call/request rows are blank. Preserve the degraded extraction of the request number, **;-:;m t;- ft2 t.t 53 1, e-A**, beside the handwritten number. | Search and assignment events in the agency control system and regional workpapers. Blank spaces in this particular copy leave the underlying activity open. [NARA cover sheet, NAID 7600768](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7600768) |
+| AEA-2597, p. 1 | The catalog describes **Folder #57** and Commission responses. The released object is one image page with a folder face and a handwritten **9/11 Commission Responses** label. Its text layer has zero lines. It contains zero standard embedded files and zero FileAttachment annotations in the tested PDF. | The item-level folder contents, index and association with any specific request or transmittal. The title and folder face are preserved as custody leads. [NARA folder scan, NAID 7600996](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7600996) |
+
+AEA-2289's page face reads **RESPONSE TO BE COORDINATED**, while the corresponding embedded field reads **RESPONSE fOBE COORDINATI!fi**. The requested April scope, Headquarters routing date, and empty regional form fields are distinct observations. Keep the short control number, the regional suffix and the extraction artifacts as recorded. [Exact fields and locators](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## Comparison with the held regional and outgoing copies
+
+- **Regional response.** N90-162 cites **#2004-004537-EA, July 15, 2004** in its subject and shows the separate **JUL 26 2004** stamp. Its embedded stamp text gives **JUL 2s m**. The memo reports a review and an estimate for copying Commission-related material. The April request and the May mailing target remain distinct from the July regional subject and stamp. The actual regional tasking that connects those stages remains unacquired. N90-162 p. 1 lines 8–10 and 19–34. [Regional response and copying review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/6cb41100f9300b81718e961493e77b729640f8c7/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-n90-national-foia-response-2026-11-09/README.md)
+- **Outgoing file copy.** AWA-572 p. 1 lines 13–23 acknowledges the **April 8** request **2004-004537** and the **August 13** request **2004-007463**. It describes its initial response as addressing the August request. The April request body confirms the distinct April scope independently of the later description. A dated final response or recipient copy keyed to the April request would test whether and when those requested records were supplied. [AWA-572 packet comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/a08578388e41fee10d66c4b15ecbe77d9ae83abd/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-awa572-response-packet-copies-2026-11-09/README.md)
+
+The **5-17-04** instruction and later regional work raise a bounded question about what happened between those records. They leave room for multiple assignments, a partial response or extensions. The outgoing register and any dated recipient copy could distinguish those possibilities. The April requester sought records previously provided to the Commission. The resulting FOIA file and the Commission's original intake are separate delivery chains. [Request source](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7600766) · [Regional memo](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7603366)
+
+## Verification and next records
+
+Verified three exact catalog/PDF pairs and their recorded SHA-256 values, two held comparator hashes, **20** text anchors and **nine** selected images or crops. The new scans contain four physical pages. The cover sheet has seven call/request pairs, with the blank fields checked visually. Standard embedded files and attachment annotations were checked on all four new pages. The test concerns the released PDF objects. [Reproducible checks and limits](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+Seek the AOA-10 outgoing-control record, actual signed reply and enclosure inventory keyed to **04-4537**, and the regional tasking and roll-up under **2004-004537-EA**. The finding aid separately lists **AEA-2598** for a New York Center certified index and **AEA-2600** for the rerecordings requested for the Commission. Join the actual item records before attributing them to folder 57 or a particular delivery. The corrected May 2003 FAA answer and dated Commission acknowledgment, signed administrative decision and recommendation-specific outcomes remain open. [Finding aid, box 112](https://www.archives.gov/research/foia/faa-finding-aid-108-126)
